    "title": "Concept: Binomial Nomenclature",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Binomial nomenclature is the <strong>two-part naming system</strong> used to give a unique and universal scientific name to every living organism. It includes the <em>Genus</em> name, which is capitalized, followed by the species name, which is lowercase. Both names are <em>italicized</em>. For example, humans are named <strong>Homo sapiens</strong>.</p>",
